"preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "Salt and freshly ground pepper to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt and freshly ground pepper to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Place the mushrooms, shallots and butter in a heavy saucepan. Cover and cook over low heat until the mushrooms are tender, about 10 minutes."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Add the potatoes, stock and white wine. Simmer, covered, until the potatoes are very soft, about 30 minutes. Add the clams and half-and-half and simmer uncovered, stirring from time to time, about 10 minutes longer."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Season to taste with salt and pepper and serve."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 236.1, "protein_g": 12.7, "carbohydrates_g": 12.1, "fat_g": 13.9, "saturated_fat_g": 8.2, "trans_fat_g": 0.4, "cholesterol_mg": 55.6, "sodium_mg": 543.1, "fiber_g": 1.0, "sugar_g": 4.5, "unsaturated_fat_g": 4.7, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": ["main course"], "meal": ["dinner"], "occasion": [], "other": ["clam juice", "mushroom", "one pot", "saute"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 10}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1991-09-08", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T00:33:49.747855+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "clams-in-black-bean-sauce", "nyt_id": 11811, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/11811-clams-in-black-bean-sauce", "name": "Clams in Black-Bean Sauce", "author": "Nicole Mones", "description": "“Clams in black-bean sauce is another American mainstay: bright, piquant, boasting more loudly of its flavorings than of its clams,” Nicole Mones wrote in The New York Times Magazine in 2007. Adapted from her husband, Paul, this recipe comes together quickly. Salted black beans are paired with bright aromatics, a wine-infused broth and briny clams, possibly the best part. As Ms. Mones wrote, “Discovering the baby clams at the bottom in their little bath of broth is the dish’s final delight.” Nicole Mones", "servings": {"text": "Serves 4", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 20, "raw": {"total": "About 20 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 teaspoon cornstarch", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "cornstarch", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "2 tablespoons salted black beans", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "salted black beans", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "2 tablespoons peanut oil", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "peanut oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "3 garlic cloves, minced", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "garlic cloves", "preparation": "minced", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "2 scallions, finely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "scallions", "preparation": "finely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "2 tablespoons minced ginger", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "minced ginger", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 teaspoon red-pepper flakes", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "red-pepper flakes", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "2 pounds Manila or littleneck clams, scrubbed and dried", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "manila or littleneck clams", "preparation": "scrubbed and dried", "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "3 tablespoons Shaoshing wine or dry sherry", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "shaoshing wine or dry sherry", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "¾ cup unsalted chicken broth", "group": null, "quantity": 0.75, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "unsalted chicken broth", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "2 tablespoons chopped cilantro", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "chopped cilantro", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Dissolve cornstarch in 1 tablespoon warm water and set aside. Soak the salted beans in ½ cup warm water for 10 minutes. Drain, and mash coarsely with a fork."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Set a wok over high heat and pour in the oil. Add the garlic, scallions and ginger and stir-fry for 30 seconds. Add the beans and red-pepper flakes and cook for 30 seconds. Drop in the clams and stir-fry for 30 seconds, then pour in the wine and broth. Reduce heat to medium and cook, covered, until most of the clams have opened, about 2 to 3 minutes. Add the cornstarch mixture and raise heat to high. Stir and cook, uncovered, until the sauce adheres to the clams, about 2 minutes. Sprinkle in the cilantro."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 303.0, "protein_g": 35.9, "carbohydrates_g": 15.3, "fat_g": 9.3, "saturated_fat_g": 1.7, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, 